# State Machine Architecture

## Purpose
Defines state machine patterns and architectures for complex SND macro automation.

## Scope
This rule covers basic state machines, advanced state machines, state transitions, and best practices.

## Basic State Machine Pattern

Most complex macros use a state machine architecture:

```lua
-- Define states
CharacterState = {
    ready = Ready,
    state1 = State1Function,
    state2 = State2Function,
    -- ... other states
}

-- State functions
function Ready()
    -- Ready state logic
    State = CharacterState.state1
end

function State1Function()
    -- State 1 logic
    if someCondition then
        State = CharacterState.state2
    end
end

-- Main execution loop
State = CharacterState.ready
while not StopFlag do
    if not (Player.IsBusy or Svc.Condition[SomeCondition]) then
        State()  -- Execute current state
    end
    yield("/wait 0.1")
end
```

## Advanced State Machine (Crafting Scripts Pattern)

```lua
-- Complex state machine with multiple states
CharacterState = {
    ready = Ready,
    crafting = Crafting,
    goToHubCity = GoToHubCity,
    turnIn = TurnIn,
    scripExchange = ScripExchange,
    processRetainers = ProcessRetainers,
    gcTurnIn = ExecuteGrandCompanyTurnIn
}

-- State transition logic
function Ready()
    -- Check conditions and decide next state
    if Inventory.GetItemCount(CrafterScripId) >= 3800 then
        State = CharacterState.scripExchange
    elseif Inventory.GetFreeInventorySlots() <= MinInventoryFreeSlots then
        State = CharacterState.turnIn
    else
        State = CharacterState.crafting
    end
end

-- Main execution with comprehensive condition checking
State = CharacterState.ready
while not StopFlag do
    if not (Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.casting] or
            Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.betweenAreas] or
            Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.beingMoved] or
            IPC.Lifestream.IsBusy()) then
        State()
    end
    yield("/wait 0.1")
end
```

## State Machine Components

### State Definition
```lua
-- Define states as a table
CharacterState = {
    ready = Ready,
    working = Working,
    complete = Complete,
    error = Error
}
```

### State Functions
```lua
-- Each state function handles specific logic
function Ready()
    -- Check conditions
    if someCondition then
        State = CharacterState.working
    elseif errorCondition then
        State = CharacterState.error
    end
end

function Working()
    -- Perform work
    if workComplete then
        State = CharacterState.complete
    elseif errorOccurred then
        State = CharacterState.error
    end
end
```

### State Transitions
```lua
-- State transitions based on conditions
function Ready()
    if Inventory.GetItemCount(itemId) >= requiredAmount then
        State = CharacterState.processItems
    elseif Inventory.GetFreeInventorySlots() <= minSlots then
        State = CharacterState.manageInventory
    else
        State = CharacterState.gatherItems
    end
end
```

